            <ArticleTitle>Non-traumatic myositis ossificans circumscripta at elbow joint in a 9-year old child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>122-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myositis ossificans circumscripta (MOC) is a kind of self-localized, benign and tumor-like lesions often seen in adults, with approximately 75% of cases caused by trauma. We reported a case of non-traumatic MOC occurred at the elbow joint in a 9-year old child and it has been excised by surgery. After 18 months follow-up, a favorable outcome has been achieved with the Broberg-Morrey score of 100. We suggest that surgical resection should be done as soon as the diagnosis is confirmed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
